      "Explicit free-function paths, monomorphic inherent source candidates and bare generic-struct paths to unique concrete-specialization source candidates. Lifetime-only struct/enum owners additionally allow bare paths to unique receiver-free inherent declarations when unbounded impl lifetime names map one-to-one to owner arguments; unsupported siblings and enum variant names block selection. Specializations require named type arguments and no impl generics/where clause; competing unsupported inherent declarations block the candidate. No type/argument inference, visibility checking, Self/type-alias resolution, explicit generic call arguments, mixed lifetime/type parameters, concrete or bounded lifetime specializations, const/bounded/defaulted generic owners, receiver types beyond explicit parameters, adjacent-before-let bindings and trait objects, macro expansion, build-script execution or external dependency source loading.",
